  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Back when some nodes had their flow removed, it ended up causing errors until those nodes are deleted and recreated. The only problem is that while you can fix it on old graphs, you can't fix it on new graphs because it causes a null reference error that breaks everything, including the ability to save changes or compile. Here are some pictures of what happens as well as the graph that it happens on: https://drive.google.com/file/d/10CnnNFOEEq5O34o_Fr_82VPiF3uY_QZm/view?usp=sharing",
